I am preparing a capstone study on allocating a small label budget for prompt-injection detection and want to avoid duplicating EvoShield (DOI: 10.3390/math14101719).

My reading of Sections 4.1-5.4 is that the experiments compare online LLM routing/review adaptation with local and LLM baselines, vary the entropy threshold and review window, and examine an ordered cross-dataset stream.

Does the paper, supplementary material, or a newer manuscript also compare these three arms at the same number of labeled examples:
1. Adjust only a frozen detector's classification threshold using target-domain labels.
2. Add generic/source-domain labeled data and retrain.
3. Add domain-matched labeled data and retrain.

We are considering small label budgets (25, 50, 100 and 200), separately sized evaluation data, low-FPR recall, and retention on an untouched domain. We are particularly interested in benign-data adaptation rather than online attack generation.

If I have missed an overlapping experiment, could you point me to the relevant section or supplementary material? A current author manuscript would also help us verify the design directly.

